/*
  # base-uri is 'self', not 'none': /demo, /originate and /receive are
  # real directories serving a copy of index.html that carries
  # <base href="/"> so its relative assets still resolve from the root.
  # 'none' blocked that tag outright, so every asset resolved against
  # /demo/, 404ed into HTML and was rejected on MIME type - the whole
  # page rendered unstyled with no script. 'self' still stops an
  # injected base pointing at another origin, which is what the
  # directive is actually for.
  # The three Google origins are GA4 and nothing else: googletagmanager
  # serves gtag.js, and the analytics hosts receive the measurement calls.
  # Added 9 Sep 2026 with the modem data stream. Before this the page
  # loaded no third-party resource at all, which is worth knowing if the
  # analytics ever come back out - the policy should come out with them.
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://www.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.googletagmanager.com; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://*.googletagmanager.com; media-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), microphone=(self)

# Revalidate the code on every request.
#
# Cloudflare Pages' own default for .js and .css is `public,
# max-age=14400, must-revalidate` - four hours in the *browser* cache -
# while it serves HTML and .wasm at `max-age=0`. Nothing here carries a
# content hash in its filename, so those four hours mean a returning
# visitor gets today's HTML wired to yesterday's JavaScript, and the
# deploy's edge-cache purge cannot help: it clears Cloudflare's copy,
# not the one already on the visitor's disk.
#
# That is not hypothetical. The Demo button 404ed on `modem.wasm` for
# hours after the fix for it went live, because the browser kept running
# the cached `wired.js` that still resolved the URL the old way - and it
# cost most of an afternoon of diagnosis, because the deployed bytes and
# the running bytes were different things and every check of the former
# said the site was fine.
#
# `no-cache` does not mean "do not store". It means "store it, but
# always revalidate before reuse", so the normal case is a 304 with no
# body - these files are tens of kilobytes and the ETags already exist.
# The correct alternative is hashed filenames plus `immutable`, which is
# what a build step would give us; this site has no build step for its
# JS, so this is the honest version of the same guarantee.
/*.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/*.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache
